# vvaharness/skills/iac/probe.sh

Infrastructure-as-code sweep: a manifest inventory naming which platforms exist, then known-bad directive greps per platform, then cross-cutting TLS and credential literals.

Source: `vvaharness/skills/iac/probe.sh` (lines 1-127)
Executor: code (POSIX shell; read-only greps; nothing in the harness parses its output)
Called from: no harness code runs it. A model session may run it through a shell tool as `sh .vvaharness/skills/iac/probe.sh [root]`, because the lens SKILL.md or the Stage 4 prompt suggests it. Whether it is run is the model's decision.

// abstracted: lines 4-17 are the Apache 2.0 license comment.
// Output is advisory text for the model; every section prints `path:line` hits, or "(none)". The script always ends with `exit 0`, so a failed grep never surfaces as an error.

// src: vvaharness/skills/iac/probe.sh:18-127
probe(ROOT = $1 or "."):executor=code {
  // src: vvaharness/skills/iac/probe.sh:18-66 — setup and the three listing helpers
  CAP = 20
  XD = exclude directories .git, node_modules, .venv, venv, __pycache__, dist, build, .vvaharness, vendor
  Q = "['\"]"

  hits(label, pattern, ...extraGrepArgs) {   // grep -rEni, case-insensitive; "(none)" or "<total> match(es); showing up to 20" plus first CAP lines
  }
  flist(label, pattern, ...extraGrepArgs) {  // grep -rElI: sorted FILE names only; "(none)" or "<n> file(s); showing up to 20"
  }
  nlist(label, ...findNameTests) {           // find by file name, pruning .git, node_modules, vendor; sorted
  }
  // preserved: hits() is case-insensitive, so "every USER directive" also counts lower-case "user" lines in Dockerfiles, and "every FROM" counts any "from" line.
  // The SKILL marks these sections as findings when EMPTY: every USER directive, securityContext / readOnlyRootFilesystem, NetworkPolicy, audit / logging config; and cross-account trust hits without ExternalId.

  print "Candidates only. Cite file:line and the security property violated before reporting."

  // src: vvaharness/skills/iac/probe.sh:68 — printf '\n--- MANIFEST INVENTORY (an absent platform is not a finding) ---\n'
